add('B-S01','ZIKA-SPRING2016-reports','ZIKA-SPRING2016','original human experiment report; author-hosted VoR','Emily K. Vraga; Leticia Bode','https://doi.org/10.1080/1369118X.2017.1313883',vurl,'2018 issue / online2017; sha256 4ef36ee9015acc7d9c7ba223425825e001ba3243e28ec82c924d7494a2f2f836','Methods printed1342–1344; Appendix FigureA1/A2 printed1353 visually rendered; results/discussion1347–1349; refs1352','2platform×3information random between-person design;613 entrants/271 analyzed. Source vs no-source correction keeps rebuttal direction, adds Snopes/CDC preview/URL. Each feed page ≥5sec. Appendix URL Snopes /zika-virus-gmo-mosquitoes/ and CDC /zika/disease-qa.html. Seven-point misinformation agreement index, not discrete advice acceptance. Direct with-source vswithout-source contrast is not significant after Bonferroni(p=.24),despite with-source vsno-misinformationcontrol difference.','Actual live click affordance, event dictionary, participant raw rows 미확인. Appendix shows Facebook-with and Twitter-without, not same-platform paired screenshots. Control lacks the misinformation post. Cohort overlaps B-S02 inferred from identical613 spring2016 sample, both repeatparticipation43 exclusions and complementary conditions; counts merged conservatively.',['Q1','Q2','Q3','Q4','Q6'],['B-DIAG-VRAGA'],utc='2026-11-23T05:10:05.471467+00:00')
add('B-S02','ZIKA-SPRING2016-reports','ZIKA-SPRING2016','original human experiment report; same-cohort companion','Leticia Bode; Emily K. Vraga','https://doi.org/10.1080/10410236.2017.1331312','https://lbode.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/bode-and-vraga-2018-see-something-say-something-correction-of-global-health-misinformation-on-social-media.pdf','2018issue/online2017','Methods printed1134; Notes1; Appendix; Discussion1136–1137','613 total/136 analyzed. Random control45 (no misinformation post), algorithmic correction43, social correction48; both correction arms show same Snopes/CDC sources. ≥5sec/page. Three-item seven-point index.','No same misinformation/no-source comparator in this report; no binary acceptance. Full methods read; same613 recruitment frame as B-S01, no participant-ID crosswalk to prove exact overlapping persons. Do not count as independent new cohort/primary minimum work.',['Q1','Q3','Q4'],['B-DIAG-VRAGA'],False)
add('B-S03','BRODSKY2021-CIVICS','BRODSKY2021-CIVICS','original human intervention report','Jessica E. Brodsky et al.','https://doi.org/10.1186/s41235-021-00291-4','https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s41235-021-00291-4','2021 VoR; HTML sha256 b604ce4e42d8746ff52732a885d00c041c7bc00266a97dd57edc099162675a2f','Methods Participants/Materials&Procedure; Table2; scoring0–4 paragraphs','230 civics students:136 DPI five sections/94 control four sections;instructor matched. A/B four-problem forms counterbalanced;all have online task access. Training six class sessions plus three online homework. Written rationales code lateral reading attempts versus successful sourcing.','Access availability is not randomized difference; training effect cannot identify link-provision effect. Selfreport/written rationale not browser-read telemetry. Raw original truth-stratified advice acceptance not recovered.',['Q1','Q3','Q4','Q7'],['B-DIAG-BRODSKY'])
add('B-S04','BREAKSTONE2021-NUTRITION','BREAKSTONE2021-NUTRITION','original human pre-post intervention report','Joel Breakstone et al.','https://doi.org/10.37016/mr-2020-56','https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/article/lateral-reading-college-students-learn-to-critically-evaluate-internet-sources-in-an-online-course/','2021-02-23','Methods; Finding2; Appendix references','87 students in two summer2020 online nutrition sections received four one-hour modules;live web at pre/post with alternate friendsofscience/co2science task forms. Author counts3/87 lateral reading at pretest;67/87 posttest;36 of67 correct and31 incorrect/irrelevant conclusions.','No control or access difference, different sources by form. 36/67 is coding of students who attempted lateral reading, not randomized source-access effect or correct/incorrect advice acceptance.',['Q1','Q3','Q6','Q7'],['B-DIAG-NUTRITION'])
add('B-S05','PANIZZA2022','PANIZZA2021-E1|PANIZZA2021-E2','original two-experiment report','Folco Panizza et al.','https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-09168-y','https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-022-09168-y','2022-04-05; HTML sha256 3d89e5805ca00ef51711766c54dbf46a3dfe3527fcc4fc158fd5f93e4434fd3a','Experiment1 Participants/Design/Stimuli/Measures; Experiment2; Discussion; Limitations','Same live FB-like post accessible in all arms, all explicitly permitted external browsing. Random popup COR tips/incentive/control; E1 recruited2700 excluded316 mobile=2384. Six-point validity rating;author dichotomous correctness threshold but no direct integer truth×condition acceptance table recovered. Lateral reading is selfreport crosschecked against study-page exit; popup increased strategy reports yet E1 accuracy null.','Education/incentive encouragement with identical source access, excluded main access contrast under SCOPE. Exit does not prove external source read/comprehension. Missing mobile exclusions are postassignment; prereg sample mismatch to supplement requires separate annotation.',['Q1','Q3','Q4','Q6','Q7'],['B-DIAG-PANIZZA'])
add('B-S06','MCGREW2023-2024-CROSSCURRICULUM','MIDWEST-2021-22-GRADE9','original human intervention report','Sarah McGrew; Joel Breakstone','https://doi.org/10.1177/23328584231176451','https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/23328584231176451','2023 VoR','Methods&Materials;Pretest/Posttest;Scoring;Results firstparagraph;Limitations','Six biology teachers taught five one-hour lessons;some geography classes additional lessons;574 both pre/post completers. Same stems alternate different live sources (Friends of Science vs CO2Science);everyone may read laterally. COVID implementation variation.','No access manipulation or randomized no-instruction comparison. B-S07 appears subset of same broader project, treated one cohort conservatively; no row identity confirmation. General/honors group difference not source-access effect.',['Q1','Q4','Q6','Q7'],['B-DIAG-CROSSCURRICULUM'])
add('B-S07','MCGREW2023-2024-CROSSCURRICULUM','MIDWEST-2021-22-GRADE9','original assessment analysis; probable overlapping subset','Joel Breakstone; Sarah McGrew; Mark Smith','https://doi.org/10.37016/mr-2020-133','https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/article/measuring-what-matters-investigating-what-new-types-of-assessments-reveal-about-students-online-source-evaluations/','2024-02-12','Methods114–130;Findings95–112;Limitations132–135','One biology teacher,2021–22 five lessons;109 paired constructed responses;pre8 attempts andpost67 lateral attempts. Same access both occasions,random A/B pre then oppositeformpost. Four-option distractors diagnose reasoning errors;formats use differentstimuli.','Not evidence of format equivalence or randomized link access. Actual cohort match withB-S06 remains inferred,conservatively merged minimum count. Selfreported evidence use not actual browser event.',['Q1','Q3','Q6','Q7'],['B-DIAG-CROSSCURRICULUM'],False)
add('B-S08','ASLETT2024-SOTEN','ASLETT-S1-S2-overlap|ASLETT-S3|ASLETT-S4|ASLETT-S5|ASLETT-S6','original multistudy human report','Kevin Aslett;Zev Sanderson;William Godel et al.','https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06883-y','https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06883-y','issue2024-01-18/online2023-12-20;HTMLsha256 a84455db6193c3ecc42703b0114ad10901dc9d61fed61bb61a218a5b00d04ea0','Methods Surveys;Determining veracity;Studies1–5 including Balance tables and Digitaltrace;Results;ExtendedData4','S1 person random search encouragement vs no encouragement, same three-of-five articles/day on original publisher website. Finaltrue/false-or-misleading/could-not-determine. Treatment reports query and evidenceURLs. S5 different plugins with GoogleSERP and visitedURL logs;searchcompensation requirement. Professional factchecker mode defines key,κ=.42.','I2 assigned external evidence-search bundle,not fixedlinked-passage-only. Attentionchecks removeallrespondentevaluations. Assignedrosters/missing counts unknown;observed endpointsnotfullITT. S1postconsentdropout51%C/58%T;S5 20%C/62%T. S5 methods653T/508traces versus analyzed608T;preserve rather than forceagreement. Raw reconstruction owned supplement stream.',['Q1','Q2','Q3','Q4','Q5','Q6','Q7'],['B01-ASLETT'])
